AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:FOODON_03307539 "Whereas dehydration may bring the moisture content of a material down to around 2.5% or less, a natural drying process is highly dependent on humidity, ambient temperature, and the nature of materials themselves, leading various kinds of food material to have a moisture content ranging from 5% to 30% [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equilibrium_moisture_content]"@en)
